  "body_html": "<h1>Locally finite regular CW complex with cellular $G$-action</h1>\n<p>Throughout §§2–4 we fix the following data.</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$X$ is a <strong>locally finite regular CW complex</strong>. <em>Regular</em> means the attaching\n  map from the boundary of each cell to $X$ is an embedding. <em>Locally finite</em>\n  means every cell is contained in the closure of finitely many cells.</li>\n<li>$G$ is a (locally profinite) group acting <strong>continuously and cellularly</strong> on\n  $X$, i.e. $G$ permutes the set of cells and the action restricted to each cell\n  is a homeomorphism.</li>\n<li>$R$ is a coefficient ring.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>The underlying topological space of $X$ is denoted $|X|$. We write\n$[\\![X]\\!]$ for the set of cells of $X$, and $[\\![X]\\!]_d$ for the $d$-dimensional\ncells. The face relation $E \\preceq F$ holds when $E \\subseteq \\overline{F}$.</p>\n<p>Two further standing notations:</p>\n<ul>\n<li>$\\Fix_G(S) := \\{g \\in G : g \\cdot s = s \\text{ for all } s \\in S\\}$ — pointwise\n  stabilizer.</li>\n<li>$\\Stab_G(S) := \\{g \\in G : g \\cdot S = S\\}$ — setwise stabilizer.</li>\n</ul>\n<p>For a cell $E$, $\\Fix_G(E)$ and $\\Stab_G(E)$ may differ; refining the CW\nstructure can force them to agree.</p>",
